  "worked_solution": "Multiplying the $1$st row in $Y$ by the $2$nd column in $Z$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{12} & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 4 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =(-2)(5)+3(-3)+0(1) \\\\  & =-10-9+0 \\\\  & =-19.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
